1
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:29,980
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

2
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,990
- Bite My Neck -

3
00:01:37,210 --> 00:01:41,080
From here, the winger, 
Mahan, will pass to Khan.

4
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:44,290
Then Tahel will cover from this position.

5
00:01:44,290 --> 00:01:45,540
All right.

6
00:01:57,050 --> 00:02:02,190
Okay! We'll run through this play
 once Mahan and the others are back.

7
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:04,280
Let's get the championship title back.

8
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:07,630
We'll wipe the smirks off 
those Decelis guys' faces.

9
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:08,770
Right, Captain?

10
00:02:09,790 --> 00:02:11,910
Huh? Uh, sorry.

11
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:13,190
What'd you say?

12
00:02:13,510 --> 00:02:16,310
We're discussing our game 
plan for the nightball game.

13
00:02:16,310 --> 00:02:19,760
Oh, right. Yeah, I agree.

14
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:21,420
Were you even listening?

15
00:02:21,420 --> 00:02:23,250
O-Of course I was.

16
00:02:23,250 --> 00:02:24,870
Then what did we say?

17
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:29,000
Basically, I just need to score, right?

18
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:35,340
Khan, something's off about you today.

19
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,840
You've been absent-minded all day.

20
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:39,580
Th-That's not true.

21
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:40,590
Did something happen?

22
00:02:40,590 --> 00:02:42,760
N-No, nothing happened.

23
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:44,650
I'm just tired.

24
00:02:45,090 --> 00:02:46,360
I'm going to sleep.

25
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:48,310
Oh, by the way,

26
00:02:48,550 --> 00:02:50,120
this is from them.

27
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:50,820
A dog?

28
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,440
They're looking for a fight.

29
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:55,480
Apparently, it's an invitation 
to their birthday party.

30
00:02:55,910 --> 00:02:57,110
What should we do?

31
00:02:59,110 --> 00:03:01,640
We'd never go to that.

32
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,470
Who'd celebrate <i>their</i> birthday?

33
00:03:03,470 --> 00:03:04,380
Right?

34
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:07,120
But you guys said you wanted to go.

35
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,210
We were just being polite.

36
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:12,810
Are you okay?

37
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,690
You should get some rest.

38
00:03:22,690 --> 00:03:23,670
Yeah.

39
00:03:25,800 --> 00:03:26,930
Goodnight.

40
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:33,020
It must be because of the total eclipse.

41
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:35,860
But why'd it have to be a human, huh?

42
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:39,110
Still, I hope it works out.

43
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,370
You sent them an invitation?

44
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:46,550
It's not like I had a choice.

45
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:49,790
Sooha said she wanted to invite them, too.

46
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:54,540
If that's what Sooha wants, 
it's not like we can say no.

47
00:03:54,840 --> 00:03:58,590
Still, I don't like celebrating 
our birthday with werewolves.

48
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:02,350
What does Sooha even 
like about them, anyway?

49
00:04:02,350 --> 00:04:04,220
Don't ask me.

50
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:07,010
It's because they hate vampires, isn't it?

51
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,020
Yeah.

52
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:12,190
Don't remind me.

53
00:04:12,190 --> 00:04:14,210
I'll never get over it.

54
00:04:14,210 --> 00:04:15,580
Don't worry about it.

55
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:18,700
She didn't know about us 
when she said that.

56
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:25,960
If Sooha finds out what we really are, 
she'll never want to see us again.

57
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:29,410
It doesn't matter what she thinks.

58
00:04:29,410 --> 00:04:31,790
This is why I said not
 to get close to her.

59
00:04:31,790 --> 00:04:35,520
What? But I want to be friends with Sooha!

60
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:39,130
I never expected her to 
hate us that much, though.

61
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:41,990
Nobody likes us.

62
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:44,850
It's natural for a human to hate us.

63
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:47,220
And her friend was killed by vampires.

64
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:51,450
We don't hurt humans, though.

65
00:04:51,450 --> 00:04:54,270
We know that about ourselves.

66
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:58,100
But to humans, we're no 
different from other vampires.

67
00:04:58,530 --> 00:05:03,690
Telling her we're an exception 
won't solve the problem.

68
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:08,980
True. We can't force her to trust us.

69
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:13,140
It's not like anyone's ever 
believed us before.

70
00:05:13,770 --> 00:05:15,910
Then we have no choice.

71
00:05:15,910 --> 00:05:20,970
We'll tell Sooha that Solon is a vampire 
so the rest of us will be off the hook.

72
00:05:20,970 --> 00:05:21,500
Huh?!

73
00:05:21,500 --> 00:05:22,710
What?!

74
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:24,680
Solon's a vampire?!

75
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:27,720
That's right. It caught
 us by surprise, too!

76
00:05:27,970 --> 00:05:30,290
Let's not waste any time.

77
00:05:30,290 --> 00:05:31,160
Here's some firewood.

78
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:32,060
Here's a light.

79
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:35,970
Die, you horrible vampire!

80
00:05:37,070 --> 00:05:40,390
Solon, we won't forget your sacrifice.

81
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:42,730
We'll keep you in our hearts forever.

82
00:05:42,730 --> 00:05:44,280
Hey!

83
00:05:44,280 --> 00:05:47,510
Noa, why are you gathering firewood?

84
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:49,340
And Jino, why are you lighting it?

85
00:05:49,340 --> 00:05:50,940
But I gathered so much.

86
00:05:50,940 --> 00:05:51,740
I'm playing along.

87
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:53,250
You can't be serious!

88
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:56,080
Sheesh! Your sacrifice 
would solve everything!

89
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,290
Then you sacrifice yourself!

90
00:05:58,290 --> 00:06:03,750
That's enough. For now, you two will 
be the candidates for that plan.

91
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:05,170
I'm not a candidate for anything!

92
00:06:05,570 --> 00:06:08,830
In any case, let's make sure she 
doesn't find out what we are.

93
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:11,890
Yeah.

94
00:06:12,760 --> 00:06:15,470
We should avoid using our 
powers as much as possible.

95
00:06:16,070 --> 00:06:18,480
If she finds out what we are,

96
00:06:19,350 --> 00:06:22,430
we won't be able to stay here anymore.

97
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:32,690
I thought we'd get to stay 
at this school for a while.

98
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:39,080
I doubt Sooha would tell anyone even 
if she found out we're vampires.

99
00:06:39,970 --> 00:06:43,720
You don't know that.

100
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:53,680
Vampires don't feel any love at all.

101
00:06:53,990 --> 00:06:57,680
Vampires are just cold, brutal monsters!

102
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:00,100
Werewolves are way better!

103
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:02,920
No, you can't even compare them.

104
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,110
Vampires are the worst!

105
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,460
Heli.

106
00:07:13,800 --> 00:07:15,140
There you are.

107
00:07:28,290 --> 00:07:30,950
Um, I'm sorry about earlier.

108
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,510
I got so worked up.

109
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:39,930
It's fine. I know how much
 you hate vampires.

110
00:07:40,490 --> 00:07:41,770
It's only natural.

111
00:07:42,070 --> 00:07:44,520
Yeah. Thanks.

112
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:50,030
We forgot to give this to you earlier.

113
00:08:00,380 --> 00:08:04,040
Come to think of it, you said 
there was a birthday coming up.

114
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:07,820
Everyone would be glad to see you there.

115
00:08:08,150 --> 00:08:09,270
I hope you'll come.

116
00:08:09,270 --> 00:08:13,840
Of course! By the way, 
whose birthday is it?

117
00:08:14,430 --> 00:08:16,140
All of ours.

118
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:17,000
Huh?

119
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:21,140
None of us knows the day we were born.

120
00:08:21,610 --> 00:08:22,330
Oh...

121
00:08:22,690 --> 00:08:24,690
Then what's this day?

122
00:08:26,330 --> 00:08:29,550
It's the day we left the orphanage.

123
00:08:33,390 --> 00:08:37,940
After the hell we went through 
the day we fled Vanfield,

124
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:41,160
you guys still trust humans?

125
00:08:53,890 --> 00:08:55,470
Is anyone chasing us?

126
00:08:55,470 --> 00:08:57,470
No, we're good.

127
00:08:57,470 --> 00:08:58,260
There's a house!

128
00:09:12,290 --> 00:09:14,660
You ran away from the orphanage?

129
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:23,170
We don't use this storage shed.

130
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:24,700
It's safe here, so you can rest.

131
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,540
Th-Thank you.

132
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,540
It's okay. I won't tell anyone.

133
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:35,640
This will help a lot.

134
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:36,550
Yeah.

135
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:39,020
Let's leave once we've had a little rest.

136
00:09:47,250 --> 00:09:48,680
I'm hungry.

137
00:09:48,680 --> 00:09:50,250
Me, too.

138
00:09:50,250 --> 00:09:51,590
Suck it up.

139
00:09:56,370 --> 00:09:58,020
You must be hungry.

140
00:09:58,020 --> 00:09:59,530
These are just leftovers, but...

141
00:10:08,790 --> 00:10:10,790
Vampires showed up?

142
00:10:10,790 --> 00:10:13,090
We have to kill them all this instant.

143
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,980
So this is where you've been.

144
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:30,120
Didn't I tell you?

145
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,980
It's dangerous outside the orphanage.

146
00:10:34,730 --> 00:10:37,860
Now, let's go back to Vanfield House.

147
00:10:40,360 --> 00:10:44,340
We can only trust each other.

148
00:10:46,830 --> 00:10:50,920
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

149
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,920
- Dark Moon: The Blood Altar -

150
00:10:55,340 --> 00:11:00,380
Sooha, you mentioned before that 
your friend was killed by vampires.

151
00:11:00,810 --> 00:11:01,640
Yeah.

152
00:11:02,930 --> 00:11:04,510
Were you close?

153
00:11:06,840 --> 00:11:10,030
You know how I have that weird power?

154
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:14,850
It made people think I was a vampire,

155
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,950
so I was always all alone.

156
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:27,950
My parents told me never to use my power.

157
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:34,500
Chris was the only one who understood me.

158
00:11:35,750 --> 00:11:37,900
But one day...

159
00:11:37,900 --> 00:11:40,060
Chris is still inside!

160
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:41,550
You can't go in there!

161
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:42,990
Let go of me!

162
00:11:42,990 --> 00:11:45,300
Chris has a bad leg!

163
00:11:47,210 --> 00:11:48,810
Hey, you!

164
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:55,570
All I could think about was saving him.

165
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:57,340
Don't do it, Sooha.

166
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,890
If anyone sees you, 
they'll get the wrong idea.

167
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:04,310
Everyone will think you're a vampire.

168
00:12:05,650 --> 00:12:06,830
Chris!

169
00:12:06,830 --> 00:12:08,210
Chris!

170
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:11,970
"I don't care what anyone thinks."

171
00:12:11,970 --> 00:12:13,810
"I don't care what anyone says about me."

172
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:21,470
Chris!

173
00:12:21,830 --> 00:12:22,580
Hold on!

174
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:25,750
I'll save... you...

175
00:12:29,990 --> 00:12:32,580
In that moment, I thought...

176
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:33,980
I'd been given this power

177
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:39,990
so I could do this.

178
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:47,010
I believed...

179
00:12:50,590 --> 00:12:56,030
that you'd come.

180
00:13:01,730 --> 00:13:07,740
I may never find 
another friend like Chris.

181
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:17,060
He even told me to bite his neck once 
because he believed I wasn't a vampire.

182
00:13:18,440 --> 00:13:25,070
Not even I could trust myself, but he...

183
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:31,310
I could never like vampires.

184
00:13:33,530 --> 00:13:34,390
Sooha.

185
00:13:35,580 --> 00:13:37,970
Want to try biting my neck?

186
00:13:37,970 --> 00:13:38,880
Huh?

187
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,840
What?!

188
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:43,330
W-Wait, what are you talking about?!

189
00:13:43,330 --> 00:13:47,240
I mean, it's not like
 I hate you or anything...

190
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:48,110
I know.

191
00:13:48,950 --> 00:13:51,960
We were kids back then.

192
00:13:51,960 --> 00:13:54,720
The situation is totally different now.

193
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:59,230
We're on our way to 
becoming adults, you know?

194
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:02,620
I-In any case, that's that!

195
00:14:02,950 --> 00:14:03,980
So?

196
00:14:07,740 --> 00:14:09,490
Go ahead.

197
00:14:12,730 --> 00:14:14,080
No! This is too embarrassing!

198
00:14:14,080 --> 00:14:15,890
I can't do it!

199
00:14:15,890 --> 00:14:20,420
But I trust you that much, too.

200
00:14:20,420 --> 00:14:21,330
Huh?

201
00:14:24,170 --> 00:14:25,340
It's true.

202
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:27,790
Wh-What about you, Heli?

203
00:14:27,790 --> 00:14:28,340
What?

204
00:14:30,190 --> 00:14:33,510
Could you bite my neck?

205
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:37,520
Oh, uh...

206
00:14:37,750 --> 00:14:40,790
See? You think it's embarrassing, too!

207
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:42,030
Well, so do I!

208
00:14:42,030 --> 00:14:43,660
Y-You're right.

209
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:56,330
To be honest, one of the reasons I wanted 
to come to this school was its library.

210
00:14:58,830 --> 00:15:04,950
It has a lot of old books, so I thought
 I could find the vampire's weakness.

211
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:10,300
But some vampires showed up 
at the plaza the other day.

212
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:14,010
That was my first time 
actually seeing one,

213
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:17,980
and I'd never been so terrified.

214
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:19,980
I couldn't stop shaking.

215
00:15:20,550 --> 00:15:23,500
It was like my whole body froze.

216
00:15:24,050 --> 00:15:26,630
But that made me realize something.

217
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:30,940
Vampires really are monsters.

218
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:32,630
I see.

219
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:39,830
I'd better head back.

220
00:15:44,070 --> 00:15:45,590
Thanks for coming to deliver this.

221
00:15:46,370 --> 00:15:48,420
Everyone's excited to see you there.

222
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:49,650
Okay.

223
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:09,480
Mahan, how are things over there?

224
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:14,280
We still don't know where our 
missing friends were taken.

225
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:18,370
Apparently, someone saw 
vampires near this town.

226
00:16:18,590 --> 00:16:24,290
I see. We entered Decelis to 
investigate that girl's death,

227
00:16:24,290 --> 00:16:27,510
<i>but those vampires didn't 
have anything to do with it.</i>

228
00:16:27,510 --> 00:16:30,920
As if they'd ever tell you the truth.

229
00:16:31,150 --> 00:16:35,610
<i>It's a fact that vampires 
are attacking our friends.</i>

230
00:16:35,610 --> 00:16:40,910
Yeah, but I saw them fighting 
vampires the other day.

231
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:44,380
At the very least, 
they didn't seem like allies.

232
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:48,400
Either way, several werewolves 
have gone missing from town.

233
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:52,180
<i>Vampires must be involved somehow.</i>

234
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:55,780
They'll come after you, too, 
if they learn you're vampires.

235
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:58,860
Be careful when you transform.

236
00:16:58,860 --> 00:16:59,940
<i>I know.</i>

237
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:04,460
Ruslan, you'll be back in time 
for the nightball game, right?

238
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:05,370
<i>Of course.</i>

239
00:17:05,600 --> 00:17:08,340
<i>Kamil, you're not out of shape, are you?</i>

240
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:09,990
Don't worry about me.

241
00:17:09,990 --> 00:17:11,870
<i>We'll call again later.</i>

242
00:17:11,870 --> 00:17:12,510
Sure.

243
00:17:12,510 --> 00:17:13,380
<i>Bye.</i>

244
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:17,170
Huh? Khan...

245
00:17:20,050 --> 00:17:23,770
Khan might be bothered 
that he can't transform.

246
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:26,190
I don't know about that.

247
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:29,060
None of us care about that.

248
00:17:29,060 --> 00:17:32,470
We couldn't ask for 
a better leader than Khan.

249
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:33,410
Yeah.

250
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:38,900
But everyone's bothered 
by different things.

251
00:17:40,650 --> 00:17:43,290
Are you part vampire?

252
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:51,040
I don't even know what I am.

253
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:55,300
I'm not the only one. 
It's the same for the other guys.

254
00:18:08,630 --> 00:18:12,320
Are the werewolves actually coming?

255
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:15,050
They haven't responded
 to our invitation yet.

256
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:17,330
Then I bet they aren't.

257
00:18:17,330 --> 00:18:22,120
Apparently, we're still preparing 
things in case they show up.

258
00:18:24,260 --> 00:18:25,700
What do you think of this?

259
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:34,150
You've always been a great artist.

260
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:36,510
I helped with this spot around here.

261
00:18:38,540 --> 00:18:42,220
My masterpiece!

262
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:43,010
What's wrong?

263
00:18:43,380 --> 00:18:46,140
Heli dropped the cake.

264
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:47,480
I'm really sorry.

265
00:18:47,940 --> 00:18:49,260
It can't be helped.

266
00:18:49,260 --> 00:18:51,230
We still have time. Let's make a new one.

267
00:18:51,230 --> 00:18:54,390
You can't have a birthday 
party without a cake.

268
00:18:54,390 --> 00:18:56,410
We'd better go buy the ingredients.

269
00:18:56,410 --> 00:18:57,820
Let's ask Jakah to do it.

270
00:18:57,820 --> 00:18:59,110
What?!

271
00:18:59,110 --> 00:19:01,770
What do you think? Pretty nice, right?

272
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:14,020
Jakah, sorry, but we need some 
things bought in a hurry.

273
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:15,670
Sure thing. I've got this.

274
00:19:19,110 --> 00:19:21,340
Huh? Is it burnt?

275
00:19:24,180 --> 00:19:25,510
Thanks for waiting.

276
00:19:27,110 --> 00:19:28,520
You saved the day.

277
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:31,390
It's convenient having Jakah 
around at times like this.

278
00:19:32,100 --> 00:19:33,470
There's no ramen.

279
00:19:33,470 --> 00:19:34,150
What?

280
00:19:34,150 --> 00:19:36,270
That wasn't on the list.

281
00:19:36,270 --> 00:19:39,060
Heli, did you forget to write it down?

282
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:42,030
Do we even need ramen?

283
00:19:42,670 --> 00:19:43,950
But...

284
00:19:44,610 --> 00:19:46,530
I really want ramen...

285
00:19:48,210 --> 00:19:50,360
I have to go out again?!

286
00:20:29,010 --> 00:20:30,080
It's nearly time.

287
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:40,080
Hey, Sooha!

288
00:20:40,080 --> 00:20:41,280
Welcome.

289
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:42,820
We've been waiting for you!

290
00:20:44,670 --> 00:20:46,470
What a lovely place.

291
00:20:46,470 --> 00:20:48,300
Thanks for coming.

292
00:20:48,300 --> 00:20:51,220
I bet it was tough getting out here
 to the middle of the woods.

293
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:55,900
No, it was fine. I was surprised, though.

294
00:20:56,250 --> 00:21:00,170
I didn't expect to find a beautiful 
mansion this deep in the woods.

295
00:21:00,170 --> 00:21:02,280
Right? I built it.

296
00:21:02,280 --> 00:21:06,170
Actually, we were just fortunate 
enough to inherit it.

297
00:21:06,170 --> 00:21:08,160
What? From who?

298
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:12,990
There was someone who supported 
us after we left the orphanage.

299
00:21:12,990 --> 00:21:14,460
Oh...

300
00:21:14,460 --> 00:21:20,100
They did a lot for us, but they passed 
away, so we inherited this place.

301
00:21:20,100 --> 00:21:21,910
I see.

302
00:21:21,910 --> 00:21:26,680
Since we live in the dorms, we only make 
it out here on weekends and summer break.

303
00:21:27,370 --> 00:21:29,980
The garden is beautiful, too.

304
00:21:30,430 --> 00:21:32,180
I maintain it.

305
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:33,740
That's a lie, too.

306
00:21:33,740 --> 00:21:36,010
Come in. I'll show you around.

307
00:21:39,790 --> 00:21:40,770
Sooha.

308
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:43,940
Khan!

309
00:21:44,220 --> 00:21:46,120
H-Hey.

310
00:23:34,490 --> 00:23:39,890
<i>Next time, Episode 6: 
"Hunter's Moon: Birthday Party."</i>

311
00:23:36,950 --> 00:23:40,250
- Birthday Party -

